HOLY FUCK I LOVE ARCEE. The Trinity Builders Program is a community credit grant that provides developers, researchers, and open-source builders with free inference access to Trinity models on the API.

The goal is to lower the barrier for using open weights, enabling users to run experiments, iterate, and ship real systems. This program is aimed at open-source projects, research initiatives, prototypes, production applications, and developer tooling. Grants range from less than 50 million tokens to over 1 billion tokens, based on the submitted project. Applications will be reviewed on a best-effort basis, with allocations depending on compute capacity and other priorities.

@arcee_ai: "We can't wait to see what the community builds with Trinity."

There's GPU rich and there's this. We push Prefill/Decode disaggregation beyond a single cluster: cross-datacenter and heterogeneous hardware, unlocking the potential for significantly lower cost per token. This was previously blocked by KV cache transfer overhead. The key enabler is our hybrid model (Kimi Linear), which reduces KV cache size and makes cross-DC Prefill/Decode practical.

Validated on a 20x scaled-up Kimi Linear model, it achieves 1.54× throughput and a 64% reduction in P90 token transfer time, directly translating into lower token cost.

@Kimi_Moonshot: "More in Prefill-as-a-Service."

Feedback on removing Preview was strongly in favor of keeping a paid option. As such, we’ll offer it at a very low price and keep it available for as long as we can justify it. We’ve also improved Thinking API reliability and lowered the output price from $0.90 to $0.80.

@arcee_ai: "Two pricing updates for the Trinity ecosystem just went live: Trinity-Large-Preview is here to stay. Rather than sunsetting the endpoint, it will now run at $0.15/M in, $0.45/M out. Trinity-Large-Thinking is dropping from $0.90/M to $0.80/M. You can access both models now via @OpenRouter or directly through our platform."

The linked OpenRouter platform provides access to various arcee-ai models, allowing users to compare pricing, context windows, benchmarks, and capabilities.

